IMPORT prelude

-- Ontario Works Act, 1997 (S.O. 1997, c. 25, Sched. A) and its General regulation (O. Reg. 134/98) -- income assistance
-- for a benefit unit in its own home: who is eligible (Act s 7 (3); O. Reg. 134/98 s 11), the asset limit (s 38 (1)
-- (a)-(d)), the monthly budgetary requirements (s 41 (1), with s 42 shelter), income and the earnings exemption (ss 48,
-- 49), the amount of assistance (s 40 (1)), and the time limits for an internal review and an appeal (Act ss 27, 28;
-- O. Reg. 134/98 ss 69, 70, 72).
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE, in the regulation's own terms: "applicant or recipient", "benefit unit", "dependant", "budgetary
-- requirements". The applicant's questions are in on-ow-seat.l4.
--
-- Edition: Act, e-Laws consolidation from 2025-07-01 (last amendment 2024, c. 28, Sched. 25, s. 8), with the 2021, c. 25,
-- Sched. 21 amendments not in force; O. Reg. 134/98, consolidation from 2026-08-13 (last amendment O. Reg. 276/26); both to
-- the e-Laws currency date 2026-10-14, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/.
-- © King's Printer for Ontario, 1997 (the Act) and 1998 (O. Reg. 134/98). NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION: the words quoted in
-- comments are from an unofficial reproduction of the consolidated law published on e-Laws; official copies are those
-- described in the Legislation Act, 2006.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Ontario Works -- income assistance for a benefit unit`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `board and lodging, a long-term care home, a hostel or a community residence (O. Reg. 134/98 ss 43, 44) is not encoded`
    `a child in shared custody halves the child's amounts (s 44.2), which is not encoded`
    `an applicant for ODSP takes the ODSP asset limit (s 38 (2)), which is not encoded`
    `assistance on behalf of a dependent child only (s 11 (2), (4); s 38 (1) (e)) is not encoded`
    `a sponsored immigrant living with the sponsor (s 51) is not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess of` x `over` y MEANS max 0 (x MINUS y)

§§ `The benefit unit`

-- s 1 (1): "dependant" is the spouse, a dependent child or a dependent adult (s 2 (1), (3)) residing in the same dwelling;
-- "child" means a person under 18; "single person" means a person with no dependants; "sole support parent" a person with
-- one or more dependants and no spouse included in the benefit unit. The unit is the applicant or recipient and the
-- dependants. Who is a spouse (s 1 (1) (a)-(d)) and who is a dependent adult (s 2 (1), (2)) are asked as facts.
DECLARE `Benefit unit` HAS
    `has a spouse included`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `dependent adults`             IS A NUMBER  -- 18 or older, other than the spouse (s 2 (1))
    `dependent children`           IS A NUMBER  -- under 18 (s 2 (3))

GIVEN `unit` IS A `Benefit unit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependants other than a spouse` MEANS (`unit`'s `dependent adults`) PLUS (`unit`'s `dependent children`)

GIVEN `unit` IS A `Benefit unit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the benefit unit size` MEANS 1 PLUS (IF `unit`'s `has a spouse included` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (`the dependants other than a spouse` `unit`)

§§ `Act s 7 (3); O. Reg. 134/98 s 11 -- eligibility`

-- s 11 (1): "A dependent adult is not eligible for income assistance on his or her own behalf." s 11 (3): a person
-- "who resides in the same dwelling place as his or her parent is not eligible ... on his or her own behalf unless he or
-- she is financially independent within the meaning of subsection 2 (2)".
GIVEN `is a dependent adult of someone in the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lives with a parent and is not financially independent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply on his or her own behalf` IF
        (NOT `is a dependent adult of someone in the household`)
    AND (NOT `lives with a parent and is not financially independent`)

-- Act s 7 (3): "No person is eligible for income assistance unless, (a) the person is resident in Ontario; (b) the
-- budgetary requirements of the person and any dependants exceed their income and their assets do not exceed the
-- prescribed limits ...; (c) the person and the prescribed dependants provide the information and the verification of
-- information required ...; and (d) the person and the person's dependants meet any other prescribed conditions".
-- (c) and (d) (including participation and pursuing other financial resources, s 13) are asked as one fact.
GIVEN `resident in Ontario` IS A BOOLEAN
      `budgetary requirements` IS A NUMBER
      `income` IS A NUMBER
      `assets` IS A NUMBER
      `asset limit` IS A NUMBER
      `provides the information and meets the other prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for income assistance under s 7 (3)` IF
        `resident in Ontario`
    AND `budgetary requirements` GREATER THAN `income`
    AND `assets` AT MOST `asset limit`
    AND `provides the information and meets the other prescribed conditions`

§§ `O. Reg. 134/98 s 38 (1) -- the asset limit`

-- s 38 (1): "(a) if the applicant or recipient is a single person, $10,000; (b) if the applicant or recipient has a spouse
-- included in the benefit unit and there are no other dependants, $15,000; (c) ... a spouse ... and one or more other
-- dependants, $15,500 for the applicant or recipient, the spouse and one other dependant plus $500 for each additional
-- dependant; (d) ... no spouse ... and one or more dependants, $10,500 for the applicant or recipient and one dependant plus
-- $500 for each additional dependant".
GIVEN `unit` IS A `Benefit unit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed limit for assets` MEANS
    LET `others` MEANS `the dependants other than a spouse` `unit`
    IN  IF `unit`'s `has a spouse included`
        THEN IF `others` EQUALS 0
             THEN 15000
             ELSE 15500 PLUS (500 TIMES (`others` MINUS 1))
        ELSE IF `others` EQUALS 0
             THEN 10000
             ELSE 10500 PLUS (500 TIMES (`others` MINUS 1))

§§ `O. Reg. 134/98 s 41 (1) -- budgetary requirements`

-- s 41 (1) para 1, the basic needs Table. Read by its rows, the amount turns on the number of dependants 18 or older:
-- with no spouse, $343 with no dependants, $360 with children only, $623 with one adult dependant, $781 with two, $956
-- with three; with a spouse, $494, $652, $826 and $1,001. "For each additional dependant, add $175 if the dependant is 18
-- years of age or older or $0 if the dependant is 0 to 17 years of age." (NOTES.md finding 3 on four or more dependants.)
GIVEN `unit` IS A `Benefit unit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable for basic needs` MEANS
    LET `adults` MEANS `unit`'s `dependent adults`
        `children` MEANS `unit`'s `dependent children`
        `beyond three` MEANS `the excess of` `adults` `over` 3
        `table` MEANS
            IF `unit`'s `has a spouse included`
            THEN BRANCH
                     IF `adults` EQUALS 0 THEN 494
                     IF `adults` EQUALS 1 THEN 652
                     IF `adults` EQUALS 2 THEN 826
                     OTHERWISE 1001
            ELSE BRANCH
                     IF `adults` EQUALS 0 AND `children` EQUALS 0 THEN 343
                     IF `adults` EQUALS 0 THEN 360
                     IF `adults` EQUALS 1 THEN 623
                     IF `adults` EQUALS 2 THEN 781
                     OTHERWISE 956
    IN  `table` PLUS (175 TIMES `beyond three`)

-- s 41 (1) para 2: "If the applicant or recipient resides north of the 50th parallel and is without year round road
-- access", by dependants other than a spouse: 0: $272 / $403; 1: $430 / $502; 2: $526 / $602; "For each additional
-- dependant, add $102."
GIVEN `unit` IS A `Benefit unit`, `north of the 50th parallel without year round road access` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the northern allowance` MEANS
    IF (NOT `north of the 50th parallel without year round road access`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE LET `others` MEANS `the dependants other than a spouse` `unit`
             `extra` MEANS 102 TIMES (`the excess of` `others` `over` 2)
         IN  IF `unit`'s `has a spouse included`
             THEN BRANCH
                      IF `others` EQUALS 0 THEN 403
                      IF `others` EQUALS 1 THEN 502
                      OTHERWISE 602 PLUS `extra`
             ELSE BRANCH
                      IF `others` EQUALS 0 THEN 272
                      IF `others` EQUALS 1 THEN 430
                      OTHERWISE 526 PLUS `extra`

-- s 42 (2) para 2, the maximum monthly shelter allowance by benefit unit size: 1: $390; 2: $642; 3: $697; 4: $756; 5: $815;
-- 6 or more: $844.
GIVEN `size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum amount payable for shelter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `size` AT MOST 1 THEN 390
        IF `size` EQUALS 2  THEN 642
        IF `size` EQUALS 3  THEN 697
        IF `size` EQUALS 4  THEN 756
        IF `size` EQUALS 5  THEN 815
        OTHERWISE 844

-- s 42 (2): "3. ... the amount payable for shelter shall be the lesser of the amount determined under paragraph 1 [the
-- actual cost] and the maximum amount ... 4. If the cost of energy for heat exceeds the maximum amount payable for shelter
-- under paragraph 2, the cost payable for shelter shall be the cost of energy for heat." Shelter costs are those listed in
-- s 42 (1) (rent, mortgage, taxes, insurance, condominium fees, utilities, heat).
GIVEN `unit` IS A `Benefit unit`, `actual shelter cost` IS A NUMBER, `of which the cost of energy for heat` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable for shelter` MEANS
    LET `maximum` MEANS `the maximum amount payable for shelter` (`the benefit unit size` `unit`)
    IN  IF `of which the cost of energy for heat` GREATER THAN `maximum`
        THEN `of which the cost of energy for heat`
        ELSE min `actual shelter cost` `maximum`

-- s 41 (1) para 4: a special diet allowance, for each member who needs one because of a listed medical condition, "the
-- lesser of ... the sum of the amounts determined by the administrator ... and ... $250". The administrator's amounts are
-- inputs, one per member.
GIVEN `amounts determined for each member` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special diet allowance` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN x YIELD min x 250) `amounts determined for each member`)

DECLARE `Allowance facts` HAS
    `north of the 50th parallel without road access` IS A BOOLEAN
    `actual shelter cost`                           IS A NUMBER
    `cost of energy for heat`                       IS A NUMBER
    `special diet amounts`                          IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `members 65 or older`                           IS A NUMBER
    `members pregnant or breast-feeding needing a non-dairy diet` IS A NUMBER
    `other members pregnant or breast-feeding`      IS A NUMBER

-- s 41 (1): the budgetary requirements "shall be equal to the sum of" paras 1 to 6: basic needs; the northern allowance;
-- shelter; the special diet allowance; "$44 with respect to each member of the benefit unit who has attained the age of 65
-- years" (para 5); and a nutritional allowance while pregnant or breast-feeding (to the infant's 12 months) of "$50, if an
-- approved health professional confirms that the person requires a non-dairy diet, or $40, otherwise" (para 6).
GIVEN `unit` IS A `Benefit unit`, `facts` IS AN `Allowance facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the budgetary requirements under s 41` MEANS
         `the amount payable for basic needs` `unit`
    PLUS `the northern allowance` `unit` (`facts`'s `north of the 50th parallel without road access`)
    PLUS `the amount payable for shelter` `unit` (`facts`'s `actual shelter cost`) (`facts`'s `cost of energy for heat`)
    PLUS `the special diet allowance` (`facts`'s `special diet amounts`)
    PLUS (44 TIMES (`facts`'s `members 65 or older`))
    PLUS (50 TIMES (`facts`'s `members pregnant or breast-feeding needing a non-dairy diet`))
    PLUS (40 TIMES (`facts`'s `other members pregnant or breast-feeding`))

§§ `O. Reg. 134/98 ss 48, 49 -- income`

-- s 49 (1) para 1: monthly earnings (gross employment income, training payments, net business income) of the unit are
-- reduced by "i. the total of all deductions required by law or by the terms of employment" (income tax, CPP, EI, union
-- dues, pension contributions), "ii. $200 per adult member of the benefit unit with earnings", "iii. 50 per cent of the
-- amount by which the monthly income determined under this paragraph exceeds the total amount of exemptions ... under
-- subparagraphs i and ii", and "iv. child care expenses actually incurred" up to para 2's maximum.
-- Para 3: the reductions in ii and iii are not included when "determining whether an applicant is eligible" or the amount
-- "for the first three months", unless para 4 applies (assistance paid continuously for three months, cancelled less than
-- six months before the application, with earnings on cancellation). The reduction stops at nil.
DECLARE `Earnings facts` HAS
    `gross monthly earnings`                IS A NUMBER  -- of all adult members, under para 1
    `deductions required by law or employment` IS A NUMBER -- para 1 i
    `adult members with earnings`           IS A NUMBER  -- para 1 ii
    `child care expenses allowed`           IS A NUMBER  -- para 1 iv, within para 2

-- s 49 (1) para 2: the maximum child care expense for each child is the actual amount if paid to a licensed provider or a
-- school board's extended day program, "otherwise is $600".
GIVEN `licensed child care paid` IS A NUMBER, `other child care paid` IS A NUMBER, `children in other child care` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the child care expenses allowed` MEANS `licensed child care paid` PLUS (min `other child care paid` (600 TIMES `children in other child care`))

GIVEN `earnings` IS AN `Earnings facts`, `the ii and iii reductions apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earnings included in income` MEANS
    LET `after deductions` MEANS `the excess of` (`earnings`'s `gross monthly earnings`) `over` (`earnings`'s `deductions required by law or employment`)
        `flat exemption` MEANS 200 TIMES (`earnings`'s `adult members with earnings`)
        `after ii` MEANS `the excess of` `after deductions` `over` `flat exemption`
        `after iii` MEANS IF `the ii and iii reductions apply`
                          THEN `after ii` MINUS (0.5 TIMES `after ii`)
                          ELSE `after deductions`
    IN  `the excess of` `after iii` `over` (`earnings`'s `child care expenses allowed`)

-- s 49 (1) paras 3, 4: whether the ii and iii reductions apply.
GIVEN `determining an applicant's eligibility or the first three months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `para 4 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the earnings exemptions apply` IF
        (NOT `determining an applicant's eligibility or the first three months`)
    OR  `para 4 applies`

-- s 48 (1): income is "the total amount of all payments of any nature paid to or on behalf of or for the benefit of every
-- member of the benefit unit", subject to ss 49 to 54. Unearned income (EI and CPP benefits are not earnings: s 49 (2),
-- (3)) counts in full; the payments ss 52 and 53 exempt (among them the Canada child benefit, the GST/HST credit, the
-- Canada workers benefit, the Ontario Trillium Benefit and the Canada disability benefit) are left out of the input.
GIVEN `earnings included` IS A NUMBER, `other income not exempt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income of the benefit unit` MEANS `earnings included` PLUS `other income not exempt`

§§ `O. Reg. 134/98 s 40 (1) -- the amount of income assistance`

-- s 40 (1): "calculated on a monthly basis by determining the budgetary requirements ... reducing that amount in
-- accordance with sections 44.2 to 47.2 and subtracting from that amount the income of the benefit unit". The ss 44.2 to
-- 47.2 reductions (shared custody, custody, hospital, treatment, OCB retroactive payments) are not encoded; a case that
-- reaches s 44.2 answers not covered in the seat.
GIVEN `budgetary requirements` IS A NUMBER, `income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of income assistance` MEANS `the excess of` `budgetary requirements` `over` `income`

§§ `Internal review and appeal (Act ss 27, 28; O. Reg. 134/98 ss 69, 70, 72)`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant or recipient`
    `the administrator`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `request an internal review in writing`
    `complete the internal review and give the decision`
    `file a notice of appeal with the Social Benefits Tribunal`

-- Act s 27 (1): "No appeal may be commenced unless an internal review has been requested." O. Reg. 134/98 s 69 (1): "The
-- prescribed time for requesting an internal review is 30 days from the day the decision is received"; (2) "in writing".
-- s 70 (1): "The prescribed time for completing an internal review is 30 days from the day the administrator receives the
-- request". Act s 28 (1) and O. Reg. 134/98 s 72 (1): an appeal within "30 days from the day the administrator's decision
-- is final". Time runs in days from the day the decision is received. The person's steps are options, written as DO
-- with LEST FULFILLED: taking the step in time moves to the next one; letting the time pass ends the matter without any
-- breach (a MAY would move on to its HENCE even when unused). The administrator's step is a duty (MUST). The one-year
-- outer limit (s 72 (2)), the Tribunal's power to extend time (Act s 28 (2)) and the administrator's power to hear a late
-- request (s 69 (3)) are not modelled here.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the internal review and appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
    DO    `request an internal review in writing`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY `the administrator`
           MUST  `complete the internal review and give the decision`
           WITHIN 30
           HENCE (PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
                  DO    `file a notice of appeal with the Social Benefits Tribunal`
                  WITHIN 30
                  HENCE FULFILLED
                  LEST  FULFILLED)
           LEST  BREACH BY `the administrator` BECAUSE "internal review not completed within 30 days of the request (O. Reg. 134/98 s 70 (1))")
    LEST  FULFILLED
